# Code Style

- Write all comments in English.
- Class/function-level: describe purpose and contract. Inline: explain **why**, not what. (Bad: `Loop users` | Good: `Adults only per policy §4.2`)
- **No end-of-line comments.** Place comments on a separate line above the relevant code.
- Auto-format **only changed files** using the project's formatter. Fall back to sensible defaults if none configured.
- When fixing or optimizing, **minimize the diff** — no unrelated reformatting, reordering, or renaming.
- **End files with a newline** (POSIX standard). All text files should have exactly one trailing newline.
